      "message": "fix(post): refuse a rotated work offset by name instead of posting it unrotated\n\nThe post stream carries only the offset's translation (OriginX/Y/Z), so a\nG54 given a rotation (SetWcsOrigin, 3-2-1 alignment) posted world-axis\ncoordinates turned against the part, silently. The verification gate now\nrefuses every rotated offset a posted op uses, naming the setup, the\nG-word, the angle and axis, and the operations. Offsets within 1e-9 rad\nof identity post byte-identical to before. The slot law is shared by\nwcs_context and the new clause.\n\nFixes #315\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
